{"schema":2,"id":"KH0043","investigatorId":"AS35A","provenance":null,"discoveredBy":null,"discoveredOn":null,"collection":{"name":"Brooklyn Museum","city":"Brooklyn, NY","country":"USA"},"notes":"1. AS35A-AS35D is a collection of 4 quipus that are tied together. The main cords are connected consecutively: AS35A to AS35B; AS35B to AS35C; AS35C to AS35D. 2. AS35A has one group of 3 pendants with values seperated by a space from 13 blank pendants. The 13 pendants are divided into groups of 4, 4, and 5 pendants by color. 3. The 4 quipus make use of the same colors alone or in combination: YB is found on all 4; MB and R are on A and D; KB is on B and D; YG is on A and C; and G is on C and D. 4. The values on AS35D repeat values on AS35A and B. The values on AS35A are limited to 17, 11, 14, and the first 3 pendant values on AS35D are 12 with a subsidiary of 5 (total 17), 11, 14. AS35B is limited to 4 values - 10, 22, 26, 34 - and the second group of pendants on AS35D have the same colors and the quite similar values of 10, 21, 26, 34. correction to 2: \"AS35A has one group of 3 pendants","primaryCord":{"length":26.5,"color":"YB","beginning":"T","termination":"K","notes":""},"cords":[{"parent":null,"level":1,"up":false,"position":4.0,"positionRecorded":true,"length":19,"color":"YB","colorOperator":":","color2":"YG","termination":"K","twist":null,"attachment":null,"fiber":null,"group":1,"knots":[{"position":3,"type":"S","count":1,"value":10,"direction":null},{"position":10,"type":"L","count":1,"value":7,"direction":null}],"note":""},{"parent":null,"level":1,"up":false,"position":4.5,"positionRecorded":true,"length":19,"color":"MB","colorOperator":null,"color2":null,"termination":"K","twist":null,"attachment":null,"fiber":null,"group":1,"knots":[{"position":3,"type":"S","count":1,"value":10,"direction":null},{"position":10,"type":"E","count":1,"value":1,"direction":null}],"note":""},{"parent":null,"level":1,"up":false,"position":5.0,"positionRecorded":true,"length":19.5,"col